From ddb135fbae3582d38cb42941f3657e897f3325d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:31:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: eon: enable dual read for the EN25QH32

The EN25QH32 has no SFDP table, so without a flag in the flash table the
core reads it with the plain 0x03 opcode on one data line, whatever the
controller and the device tree allow. Its sibling EN25QH64 is already
listed with SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ; the EN25QH32 is the same family and supports
the Dual Output Fast Read (0x3b).

Only dual read is enabled. The 4 KiB erase of the EN25QH64 entry is left
out so the erase layout of the 4 MiB part does not change.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
index a3b57a6..8332dad 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ static const struct flash_info eon_nor_parts[] = {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x70, 0x16),
 		.name = "en25qh32",
 		.size = SZ_4M,
+		.no_sfdp_flags = SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ,
 	}, {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x70, 0x17),
 		.name = "en25qh64",
-- 
2.43.0

